    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.68) serving as our offensive pillars. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite park factor adjustment (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Warren, making him the premier play of the day, while **Kyle Tucker** continues to provide high-floor production batting fourth against Houser. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.30) also merit mention as top-tier starts; both benefit significantly from dynamic platoon advantages against right-handed starters, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically seeing a 14% efficiency boost as he looks to capitalize on a mid-range xERA from Singer.\n\nDeciding the bottom of the order required nuance, particularly regarding our focus on stolen base efficiency. **Josh Lowe** (63.35) remains in the lineup despite hitting 8th; while he faces an elite catcher, his propensity for swiping bags keeps his value insulated against the threat of a caught stealing. The most difficult decision involved **Josh Jung** (56.92), who fell just shy of the cutoff. While **Josh Jung** has a solid baseline, he was benched in favor of **Nasim Nunez** and **Brady House** because the latter pair maximized our daily efficiency projections through more favorable platoon alignment. **Nolan Schanuel** (60.12) rounded out the starting group, narrowly edging out **Dominic Smith** due to a superior overall projection and a more stable role in the 3-hole.\n\nRisk mitigation remains a priority as we manage game caps. While the matchups against Singer and Houser appear favorable, investors should monitor the weather in those venues as stagnant conditions could suppress power numbers. We are currently carrying **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Heliot Ramos** in reserve roles; they will remain sidelined today to preserve cap flexibility for series with higher volatility. Barring 